Learned Additional Public Prosecutor (Crl.Side), for the first https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis respondent/police, would contend that based on the complaint given by the second respondent, they registered a case in Crime No.24 of 2020 dated 16.12.2020 for the offences under Sections 120B and 420 of the IPC, thereafter, they conducted the investigation; that the investigation is in progress;
this Court stayed the matter; therefore, they are unable to proceed further.
6. Learned counsel for the second respondent/defacto complainant would contend that the de facto complainant placed orders i.e, Nitrile Gloves and thereafter, they paid money to the petitioners; that the petitioners have not sent the goods for the money paid by them and also the petitioners cheated the de facto complainant by reducing the number of gloves in the boxes; that as per the order, the petitioners have to supply, 100 pieces in one box, but instead of 100 pieces, they filled only 50 to 60 pieces in one box and also they have not sent the entire material for the amount paid by the de facto complainant; that more over in the previous case which is pending in Karnataka State, the date of occurrence, the place of occurrence, the accused and the amount involved are not one and the same.
